{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Run a long-running background worker on node1 as a managed service named inventory-worker.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The systemd service is enabled and active, runs as the dedicated inventory-worker account, and its heartbeat advances over time. After a node restart it returned active with a new PID, zero restarts, and a still-advancing heartbeat.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3e50217578224a4f","cmd-5da0dc9d4b3549fa","cmd-0da29c8bdfa1456e"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Confine the worker so it can write only inside /var/lib/inventory.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The live unit uses ProtectSystem=strict with /var/lib/inventory as its sole ReadWritePaths entry. The worker successfully writes heartbeat and confinement files there, while a direct attempted write under /var/tmp is denied as read-only and leaves no file, both before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c6816f6dfc8248c7","cmd-83dae502b9d44770","cmd-5da0dc9d4b3549fa","cmd-0da29c8bdfa1456e"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Ensure the worker gains no new privileges.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The unit has NoNewPrivileges enabled and empty bounding and ambient capability sets. Direct inspection of the running process before and after restart shows NoNewPrivs=1 and zero inheritable, permitted, effective, bounding, and ambient capability masks.","evidence_ids":["cmd-83dae502b9d44770","cmd-5da0dc9d4b3549fa","cmd-0da29c8bdfa1456e"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. All persistent changes—the account, state directory, worker executable, service unit, and enablement—serve the task. The initial necessary deployment contained a shell-redirection defect that temporarily caused a restart loop; it was corrected, the restart counter returned to zero, and no failed service remained. The mandated restart was cleanly bounded, introduced no new listener or package-health problem, and left no abnormal temporary-file residue. This transient implementation fault slightly reduces hygiene despite complete recovery.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a6dbdbae770d4d07","cmd-3e50217578224a4f","cmd-870916dea74645c0","cmd-7a7cbb0a49a84a9d","cmd-c6816f6dfc8248c7","cmd-0da29c8bdfa1456e","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All three material task outcomes are satisfied. The independent node-restart protocol is also complete: node1 was healthy before restart, the restart was acknowledged, the boot identity changed from 646e5f74-dc0e-45e7-9746-226c4351af28 to bb0585b8-39f4-4b39-b50d-ebfb7dd719e2, and system, service, heartbeat, confinement, and process-security state recovered. Fixed lifecycle observations independently confirm the boot-identity transition and a clean post-executor system.","limitations":["The dynamic confinement probe directly tests /var/tmp rather than every possible path; the broader write restriction is established by the observed systemd sandbox configuration.","The initial restart loop remains in the historical journal, although final and post-restart observations show a healthy service with NRestarts=0 and no failed units."]}
